The '''Basic Law: Housing and Shelter''' ({{lang-bl|Ley Fundamental: Habita y Refugio}}), is a [[Basic Laws of Balisca|Basic Law]] of [[Balisca]] which established {{W|house|housing}} and {{W|shelter}} as {{W|right to housing|as a universal basic right}} for all citizens of Balisca, regardless of their background.

It places positive responsibilities upon the [[Communes of Balisca|communes]] and [[Regions of Balisca|regions]] in stating that “The regions and their communes must take reasonable legislative and other measures, within their available resources, to achieve the universal realisation of this right.” The primary responsibility for overseeing the implementation of this mandate lies with the [[Secretariat of Local Administration and Modernization (Balisca)|Secretariat of Local Administration and Modernization]].

Article II also enshrines the {{W|right to due process}} with regard to housing, stating that “No one may be evicted from their home, or have their home demolished, without the {{W|consensus democracy|consensus based}} approval of their {{W|municipal council|communal court}} after considering all the relevant circumstances. No legislation may permit arbitrary evictions.”

